# Credit Card Financial Dashboard [Practice Project]

## Overview
This practice project is an interactive Credit Card Financial Dashboard created to analyze customer transactions, revenue trends, spending behavior, and customer demographics.

The dashboard provides insights into:
- Revenue performance
- Transaction analysis
- Customer segmentation
- Spending categories
- Card usage behavior
- Customer income and education analysis

---

# Dashboard Screens

## 1. Credit Card Transaction Report
The Transaction Report dashboard focuses on:
- Total Revenue
- Interest Earned
- Transaction Amount
- Transaction Count
- Revenue by Card Category
- Revenue by Expenditure Type
- Revenue by Customer Job & Education
- Revenue by Payment Type

### Key Insights
- Total Revenue: 55M
- Total Interest Earned: 8M
- Total Transactions: 656K
- Blue card category generated the highest revenue
- Swipe transactions were the most used payment method

---

## 2. Credit Card Customer Report
The Customer Report dashboard provides customer demographic analysis including:
- Revenue by Age Group
- Revenue by Gender
- Revenue by Marital Status
- Revenue by Education
- Revenue by Income Group
- Revenue by State
- Revenue by Dependent Count

### Key Insights
- Businessman customers generated the highest revenue
- High income customers contributed the most revenue
- Graduate customers generated the highest customer revenue
- Texas and New York were among the top revenue-generating states

---

# Tools & Technologies Used
- Power BI
- Excel / CSV Dataset
- PostgreSQL
- Data Visualization Techniques
- DAX Measures
- Data Cleaning & Transformation

---

# Features
- Interactive filters and slicers
- Quarterly performance analysis
- Dynamic visualizations
- Customer segmentation
- Revenue tracking
- Transaction behavior analysis

---

# Project Objective
The objective of this project is to help businesses analyze customer spending patterns and financial performance using interactive dashboards and visual analytics.

---

# How to Use
1. Download the Power BI file (.pbix)
2. Open using Power BI Desktop
3. Interact with filters and slicers
4. Explore customer and transaction insights

